*Heading
 NLVE_SCHAPERY example 02: thick-walled PA6 tube under internal pressure (axisymmetric)
** ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
** Long tube, inner radius 10 mm, outer radius 20 mm, plane strain in axial direction
** (eps_zz = 0), 20 CAX4 elements over the wall thickness. Internal pressure 12 MPa,
** applied within 5 s and held for 160 h.
**
** Why this example: for LINEAR viscoelasticity with a time-independent Poisson ratio
** (as in this model) the stresses of a load-controlled problem are time-independent
** (correspondence principle) - only the displacements creep. With the stress-dependent
** Schapery functions the most loaded inner wall becomes more compliant and creeps faster,
** so the stresses REDISTRIBUTE over time. Set the three function types (PROPS 9, 14, 19)
** to 0 to see the linear reference with constant stresses.
**
** Run:    abaqus job=tube_axi user=../../src/nlve_schapery.f interactive
** Output: S11 = radial, S22 = axial, S33 = hoop stress (CAX4 convention);
**         history output of the inner- and outermost element and of the radial
**         displacement U1 at the inner and outer surface.
** Units:  mm, N, MPa, s
** ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
